  The mark-unital check is then applied only to the terminal core: there
  the top-petal gate is exactly AP/GW, and exact M separates those from
  the loose terminal petals.

[Proof attack distilled]
  1. Existing theorem-level gates: q=2..13 covered, q=14 omitted, and
     unit residues covered. Failure here is loose-up or apex-blocked.
  2. Existing AP-tail measure theorems THM-542/543/544 close the one-tail
     and two-tail below-second AP collar; the petal attack should not redo
     those exact interval certificates.
  3. Petal lemma target: once the proof enters the minimal one-petal branch,
     the only mark-unital terminal rows are AP and 12->24. The exact escape
     witnesses are 8->16 with M=2/23 and 10->20 with M=2/27.
  4. The GW window explains why 12 is special: [14-12,27-24]=[2,3] has no
     coprime blocker for 12, while every other h has a blocker.
  5. Remaining global work: prove every primitive tight survivor either
     enters that one-petal branch or is killed by a multi-dipole/far-tail
     theorem preserving the marked Farey node.
